2.THE SPIDER STEPS 
A spider present at the bottom of the well of height H, needs to get out of it. 
The walls of the well are very slippery. In each step, it climbs U metres and slips down D metres. 
If in the last step, the spider gets out of the well by climbing U metres, it does not slip back. 
Find the number of steps the spider takes.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            static int minStep(int H, int U, int D) {
                // code here
                if(U>H){
                    return 1;
                }
                int meters=U-D;
                return (H-U+meters)/meters+1;
            }
        }
